-- title:
--   From HTo G SUS Context Avg Le One
-- statement:
--   **The averaged first-root `SUS` context has expectation at most one.**
--
--   Let `params` have a field model, let `psi_bi` be a normalized bipartite quantum state on `ι × ι`, and let `family` be an indexed polynomial submeasurement family. Assume that the uniform field average of the complete branch totals equals `family.averagedSubMeas.total`, and that the uniform field average of the incomplete branch totals equals its complement:
--
--   $$
--   \mathbb E_x\,\operatorname{completePartSubMeas}(\mathrm{params},\mathrm{family},x).\operatorname{total}=\operatorname{family.averagedSubMeas}.\operatorname{total},
--   \qquad
--   \mathbb E_x\,\operatorname{incompletePartSubMeas}(\mathrm{params},\mathrm{family},x).\operatorname{total}=1-\operatorname{family.averagedSubMeas}.\operatorname{total}.
--   $$
--
--   Then, for any natural numbers $\ell,n$, sample $q=(x,xs)$ uniformly from $\mathbb{F}_q\times\operatorname{PointTuple}(\mathrm{params},n)$, and for each pair of G-hat outcomes $g,gs$ set
--
--   $$
--   S=\operatorname{fromHToGRecurrenceWeight}(\mathrm{params},\mathrm{family},\ell,\operatorname{prependTypeBit}(g.\mathrm{isSome},\operatorname{gHatTupleType}(gs))),\quad U=\operatorname{gHatIdxMeas}(\mathrm{params},\mathrm{family},x).\operatorname{outcome}(g),\quad T=\operatorname{gHatHalfProductOutcomeOperator}(\mathrm{params},\mathrm{family},n,xs,gs).
--   $$
--
--   The resulting averaged squared norm is bounded by one:
--
--   $$
--   \mathbb E_q\sum_{g,gs}\operatorname{ev}_{\psi_{\mathrm{bi}}}\!\left(\bigl(\operatorname{leftTensor}(T)\operatorname{rightTensor}(SU)\bigr)\bigl(\operatorname{leftTensor}(T)\operatorname{rightTensor}(SU)\bigr)^{\mathsf H}\right)\le 1.
--   $$
--
--   This is the first-root context estimate used in the M2-to-M3 and M3-to-E paper moves.
--
--   Formalization credit: Sirui Lu, Ruixuan Deng, Yanqiao Zhu, and Zhengfeng Ji (arXiv:2609.19814). Mathematical source: Zhengfeng Ji, Anand Natarajan, Thomas Vidick, John Wright, and Henry Yuen (arXiv:2009.12982).
--
--   **Formalization Note.** The source declaration is `MIPStarRE.LDT.Pasting.fromHToG_SUS_context_avg_le_one`; its Lean statement gives the exact quantifier order and all boundary hypotheses.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/LionSR/MIPStarRE/blob/f382c801026f53a9efc260fdee707cb35e0adb15/MIPStarRE/LDT/Pasting/Bernoulli/FromHToG/PaperBounds/SandwichContext.lean#L243-L531

